<p>Earnings (loss) applicable</p>
<p>  to common shares	    .16	(.82)     .29     (1.16)</p>
<p>(A)  Royalties from automotive airbags ceased with the third quarter 1996 airbag litigation settlement.  Airbag royalties recorded in the first six months ended June 30, 1996 were $13.4 million. Realty sales for the six months ended June 30, 1996 were $1.5 million.  With the disposition of substantially all realty assets at the end of 1996 there were no realty sales during the first half of 1997. (B)  Earnings applicable to common shares is net earnings reduced by dividends on preferred stock in the six months ended June 30, 1997 and 1996, and further reduced by the value of additional shares issued to induce conversion of preferred stock for the six months ended June 30, 1996. (C)  Preferred stocks, all common stock equivalents, were anti-dilutive and accordingly were excluded from average outstanding shares for the quarter ended June 30, 1996 and for the six months ended June 30, 1997 and 1996.  Dividends payable on the anti-dilutive preferred stocks and the value of additional shares issued to induce conversion were deducted from net earnings before calculating the earnings per share  amount.</p>
